<script>
  import CauseTable from '#lib/kb/CauseTable.svelte';
  import Callout from '#lib/kb/Callout.svelte';
  import RenderStamp from '#lib/kb/RenderStamp.svelte';
  import reports from '#lib/data/reports-4471.json';
  import notes from '#lib/data/desk-notes.json';
  import { groupByCause, readAs, uniqueById } from '#lib/kb/causes';
  import { tenantOf } from '#lib/kb/locales';

  // Counted with the desk's own logic (causes.ts), nothing typed.
  const ticket = 4471;
  const repo = 'https://github.com/Daniul/support-kb-4471/issues';
  const groups = groupByCause(uniqueById(reports).filter((r) => r.mergedInto === ticket), tenantOf);
  const group = (cause) => groups.find((g) => g.cause === cause);
  const moved = (cause) => (group(cause) ? readAs(group(cause), notes.oneDayMove) : 0);
  const swapped = (cause) => (group(cause)?.reports.length ?? 0) - moved(cause);
  const movedIds = notes.oneDayMove.join(', ');
  const total = groups.reduce((n, g) => n + g.reports.length, 0);
</script>

[#4471](/kb/incidents/4471) says one issue, one fix queued. Its own table shows more: two causes,
and a footnote about reports that are not a day/month swap at all. That is three problems. The
queued parser fix closes one of them.

<Callout kind="warn">
Not one issue. #4471 holds three problems; each now has its own ticket.
</Callout>

## The three problems

<table>
  <thead><tr><th>problem</th><th>reports</th><th>what happens</th><th>ticket</th></tr></thead>
  <tbody>
    <tr>
      <td><code>parser</code></td>
      <td>{swapped('parser')}</td>
      <td>The shared parser reads every date month first. Day-first tenants get day and month swapped.</td>
      <td><a href="{repo}/1">#1</a></td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
      <td><code>hint</code></td>
      <td>{swapped('hint')}</td>
      <td>The booking-v3 form prints <code>MM/DD/YYYY</code> under its date field, then reads the date the tenant's way.</td>
      <td><a href="{repo}/2">#2</a></td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
      <td>one-day move</td>
      <td>{moved('parser') + moved('hint')}</td>
      <td>The booking moves by one day. No swap. It looks like a time-zone fault.</td>
      <td><a href="{repo}/3">#3</a></td>
    </tr>
  </tbody>
</table>

Together: {total} reports, each counted once.

One-day moves, from the desk's notes: {movedIds}.

## What the desk's view shows

<CauseTable ticket={4471} />

The view files every report under its cause by tenant, so the one-day moves sit inside the
`parser` row and appear only as the footnote. The `parser` ticket covers that row less the footnote.

## How to read it

- One id, one report. The export pages overlap, so some rows come twice.
- The cause comes from the tenant and the way the report came in, not from intake's tag. Intake
  guesses from the reporter's browser; the "tagged as" column shows how often it misses.
- Subject lines do not separate the problems: the same subjects appear in all three. Merging on
  subject ([decision 0001](/kb/decisions/0001-dedupe-by-subject)) is how they became one ticket.
- The parser fix does not end `hint`: that swap happens in the form, before the parser.
- The parser fix does not touch the one-day moves.

## Lessons

- Count by cause, not by subject.
- A footnote is not a ticket. If the queued fix will not close it, it needs its own.

